# Build
# build*/ rather than build/: CMakePresets.json puts the ninja preset in
# build-ninja/ and the option-off presets in build-off/.
build*/
out/
# `cmake --install --prefix dist` is the documented player-build layout in
# README.md. Its content (PNG, glTF, WAV, HLSL) is not covered by the binary
# patterns further down, so without this the documented command leaves ~36 MB
# of addable files in the tree.
dist/
cmake-build-*/
.vs/
x64/
*.user
*.suo
*.sln.docstates

# IDE / editor
.idea/
# .vscode/* rather than .vscode/: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so the three shared files below would be unreachable.
# Everything else in there stays personal.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/launch.json
.cursor/
.cursor-tmp/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# AI Management CLI — machine-local. Holds the base URL, the project slug and
# (later) an API token, plus .aim/outbox/ for writes queued while the server
# was unreachable. `aim init` recreates it; the CLI also works with no config
# at all against a localhost server holding one project.
.aim/

# Claude Code — personal/local, never shared
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/settings.local.json

# Local / secrets — never commit
# Local cvar overrides. Unanchored on purpose: the engine looks for this file in
# a discoverable repo root first, then in the content root (which is next to the
# exe in an install), so it can legitimately show up in more than one place.
config.cfg
.pp/
*.keys
.env
.env.*

# OS / tooling crash artifacts
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
*.stackdump

# Artifacts (build outputs live under build/)
*.exe
*.dll
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.obj
!packages/**/content/**/*.obj

# Shader pipeline cache
.cache/
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dylib

# Downloaded third-party scene - not engine source, and not committable to a
# public repo: ph_hidden_alley.bin alone is 239 MB. The whole directory is
# ignored rather than just the textures, and r.scene defaults empty, so nothing
# in the build or the gates depends on it being present.
packages/sandbox/content/scenes/alley/

# Personal research library — kept locally, not published (public repo).
# Schematics are figures extracted from those same papers, so they follow the
# same rule: they stay on disk, they don't go in a public MIT repo.
reasarch/*.pdf
reasarch/*.pptx
reasarch/Schematics/

# Keep *.lib out of repo root only; build/ is already ignored
